From lauriekell at googlemail.com  Fri Aug 10 15:16:34 2012
From: lauriekell at googlemail.com (Laurie)
Date: Fri, 10 Aug 2012 15:16:34 +0200
Subject: [FLR-list] Estimating Btrigger suggestions
In-Reply-To: <8FE8A24E425793428F3C772FA61961A51FBFD797@SCOMP0936.wurnet.nl>
References: <8FE8A24E425793428F3C772FA61961A51FBFD797@SCOMP0936.wurnet.nl>
Message-ID: <502509B2.5090707@gmail.com>

Btrigger is a level of biomass that if the stock falls triggers 
management action to rebuild the stock as part of a HCR.

Choosing a value that is too small will result in higher risk of stock 
collapse and loss yield since biomass will fall below BMSY, Choosing a 
value that is too high will result in loss yield due to fishing effort 
being reduced unnecessarily. Blim needs to balance these objectives. The 
best way to do this would be to conduct an MSE with appropriate 
uncertainty, i.e. try a variety of values for Btrigger and choose the 
one that performs best. If you have an MSY harvest control rule there is 
no need for an Ftrigger as you would be setting F to FMSY if B>BMSY and 
F to that given by the line joining (FMSY, Btrigger) to (Flim,blim).

Laurie




